        "text": "Technician Guide Day to day use of Rem0te: finding a computer, connecting to it, helping someone who is not enrolled, and keeping the remote control client current. Screenshots are captured from a seeded demo instance. Every business, person and computer in them is fictional. Terminology. A Business is a customer organisation and is the security boundary — a Business User only ever sees computers belonging to their business. A Computer (also called an endpoint or enrolled client) is a machine with the Rem0te agent permanently installed. See access control.md for who can do what."
