        "text": "The launch policy answers 403 with a code and a sentence; the UI shows the sentence. Most often: Code Meaning What to do / The computer's agent does not report that it can enforce view only or attended consent. No shipped agent does yet. Expected for preset backed technicians. A business member or a custom assignment with Remote connect can still connect as before. Preset backed control needs an activated temporary grant. Request it, have someone else approve it, then activate it with a fresh sign in. The computer is a domain controller, hypervisor, backup server or RMM host. Nobody can connect interactively without an approved, activated exception from a managed admin workstation. Device attestation does not exist yet, so this cannot currently be satisfied. Check the device class is right ( Settings → Security → Technician Access ). An activity limit was reached and the identity is paused. Someone else clears it under Pauses & alerts . Suppressing the alert does not lift it. / The person's tier does not include it on this computer. Use the inspector to see which grant applies. A queued inventory or event log command that ends with \"the person who requested this is no longer allowed to\" was re checked at dispatch after its requester was demoted, revoked or paused. It was never sent to the computer."
