        "text": "Staged patching rem0te 0.27 can install Windows updates on customer computers in stages. A canary computer goes first, then one or more rings . Each ring is a single signed plan that two people on the approval roster authorize with a passkey. The next ring can't be requested until the canary reports that the updates took effect. The plan is approved, delivered and executed exactly like the approved Print Spooler action: the same approval signer, roster, signature and agent checks. This page covers only what is different for updates. Warning. An installed update may not stay installable out . Some can't be uninstalled, and uninstalling is not built here. rem0te never restarts a computer, so an update that needs a restart is reported as restart required until someone restarts it."
