        "text": "These are two separate systems. Presets are not roles. They apply only to MSP technicians acting in a business through an assignment. Scope Default capabilities Interactive launch Platform Admin Every business, explicitly All Yes, with the password Business Owner Their own business All, in that business Yes, with the password Business User Their own business, per computer , on computers they are given (or company wide ones) Yes, with the password L1 Help Desk One business per assignment , No L2 Technician One business per assignment L1 + , basic diagnostics Only by temporary grant, and refused on shipped endpoints (above) L3 Senior One business per assignment L2 + advanced diagnostics, not limited to standard workstations As L2, plus Windows update deployments (high impact). Elevation is not built Custom assignment (pre 0.23, or made from a group with capabilities) One business per assignment Exactly what was granted As a Business User What an admin can restrict: clone and narrow a preset, or reset it; set dates and a weekly schedule on an assignment; limit an assignment to named computers; require Business Owner approval of assignments (off by default); tighten the platform policy at once, or loosen it through an independent reviewer. A Business Owner can tighten their own business only (consent, unattended, clipboard, file transfer, extra protected classes, shorter sessions). What no setting can change: No preset can ever grant Connect, credential reveal, edit, add, remove, Quick Connect or user management. Nobody approves their own request. Protected device classes are refused to everyone. Details: technician access.md, technicians.md, access control.md."
