        "text": "All endpoints require an API key in the header: Keys are created under Settings → Monitoring & API → API keys ( , added in 0.29 — before that the screen did not exist and keys could only be made with the admin API , which still works). A Business Owner creates keys for their own business; a Platform Admin picks the business. The raw key is shown once at creation; server side we store only a SHA 256 hash. Keys support: 1. Business — Platform Admins only; a key always belongs to one business. 2. A name you will recognise in the audit log. 3. Scopes — tick only what the integration needs. 4. Create key — the key is shown once, with a Copy button. 5. Existing keys: prefix, scopes, last use, expiry, and Revoke . name — human label businessId — the business the key belongs to. Required. A key acts as a Business Owner within that business and nowhere else ; it is never a Platform Admin. Keys created before v0.8.0 had no business and were revoked by migration — re issue them per business. scopes — one or more of , , , , , , , , expiresInDays — optional TTL (1–3650), null = never expires Revocation is immediate. Rate limited to 300 req/min per key. Every route enforces its declared scope; missing scopes → HTTP 401."
